From a5056d514a5b4b8f09bb9b8739f847bebfac3ab0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:42:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Report findings with stable rule ids, CWE on every built-in
 rule, and a code frame

- frensense-lang::rule_card: one card per sink label and built-in checker
  rule (id, title, CWE list, why, fix); taint_cwe/checker_rule_cwe now
  resolve through it, so no built-in rule ships without a CWE (tests in
  lang and packgen fail if a label has none).
- Advisory gains rule_id; SARIF groups by it (one rule per id, CWE tags,
  helpUri, security-severity, region snippet) instead of using the message
  text as the rule id.
- Terminal report prints the offending line with a caret, rule id + CWE,
  and class-specific why/fix instead of the repeated Details/Impact/
  Remediation triple.
- XPath/template/response/log/etc. sinks now carry their own CWE
  (benchmark 158/59 -> 172/59 TP/FP).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
